{"parentUuid":"bc467ea0-74e6-4d0c-b382-6877b1ae1514","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/lukin/Neumann","sessionId":"f409b145-d62e-472d-b034-4de3a5b13ab9","version":"2.1.72","gitBranch":"publish-and-snapshot-improvements","slug":"mighty-hugging-umbrella","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Kvka1WCodLNgtGjnDRH1qN","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→---\n     2→name: Benchmark PR\n     3→\n     4→\"on\":\n     5→  pull_request:\n     6→    types: [labeled, opened, synchronize]\n     7→    paths:\n     8→      - 'tensor_store/src/**'\n     9→      - 'relational_engine/src/**'\n    10→      - 'graph_engine/src/**'\n    11→      - 'vector_engine/src/**'\n    12→      - 'tensor_chain/src/**'\n    13→      - 'query_router/src/**'\n    14→      - '**/benches/**'\n    15→\n    16→permissions:\n    17→  contents: read\n    18→  pull-requests: write\n    19→\n    20→jobs:\n    21→  benchmark:\n    22→    name: Run Benchmarks\n    23→    if: >-\n    24→      github.event.label.name == 'bench' ||\n    25→      (github.event_name == 'pull_request' && github.event.action != 'labeled')\n    26→    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    27→    timeout-minutes: 45\n    28→    steps:\n    29→      - name: Checkout PR\n    30→        # v4.2.2\n    31→        uses: actions/checkout@de0fac2e4500dabe0009e67214ff5f5447ce83dd\n    32→\n    33→      - name: Try to download main baseline\n    34→        id: baseline\n    35→        # v4.3.0\n    36→        uses: >-\n    37→          actions/download-artifact@d3f86a106a0bac45b974a628896c90dbdf5c8093\n    38→        continue-on-error: true\n    39→        with:\n    40→          name: criterion-baseline\n    41→          path: target/criterion\n    42→          github-token: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}\n    43→          repository: ${{ github.repository }}\n    44→          run-id: ${{ github.event.pull_request.base.sha }}\n    45→\n    46→      - name: Checkout base branch (fallback)\n    47→        if: steps.baseline.outcome == 'failure'\n    48→        # v4.2.2\n    49→        uses: actions/checkout@de0fac2e4500dabe0009e67214ff5f5447ce83dd\n    50→        with:\n    51→          ref: ${{ github.base_ref }}\n    52→          path: base\n    53→\n    54→      - name: Install Rust toolchain\n    55→        # stable\n    56→        uses: dtolnay/rust-toolchain@f7ccc83f9ed1e5b9c81d8a67d7ad1a747e22a561\n    57→        with:\n    58→          toolchain: stable\n    59→\n    60→      - name: Cache Rust\n    61→        # v2.7.8\n    62→        uses: Swatinem/rust-cache@779680da715d629ac1d338a641029a2f4372abb5\n    63→\n    64→      - name: Install protoc\n    65→        run: >-\n    66→          sudo apt-get update &&\n    67→          sudo apt-get install -y protobuf-compiler\n    68→\n    69→      - name: Install critcmp\n    70→        run: cargo install critcmp\n    71→\n    72→      - name: Benchmark base branch (fallback)\n    73→        if: steps.baseline.outcome == 'failure'\n    74→        working-directory: base\n    75→        run: |\n    76→          cargo bench --workspace --bench '*' \\\n    77→            --exclude fuzz \\\n    78→            --exclude neumann-native \\\n    79→            --exclude integration_tests \\\n    80→            --exclude stress_tests \\\n    81→            -- --save-baseline base\n    82→\n    83→      - name: Copy cached baseline\n    84→        if: steps.baseline.outcome == 'success'\n    85→        run: |\n    86→          echo \"Using cached main baseline from artifact\"\n    87→\n    88→      - name: Benchmark PR branch\n    89→        run: |\n    90→          cargo bench --workspace --bench '*' \\\n    91→            --exclude fuzz \\\n    92→            --exclude neumann-native \\\n    93→            --exclude integration_tests \\\n    94→            --exclude stress_tests \\\n    95→            -- --save-baseline pr\n    96→\n    97→      - name: Compare benchmarks with per-crate thresholds\n    98→        id: compare\n    99→        run: |\n   100→          critcmp base pr > bench-comparison.txt 2>&1 || true\n   101→\n   102→          python3 - << 'PYEOF'\n   103→          import re\n   104→          import sys\n   105→\n   106→          # Parse bench-thresholds.toml for per-crate thresholds\n   107→          thresholds = {}\n   108→          default_pct = 15\n   109→          current_crate = None\n   110→\n   111→          with open(\"bench-thresholds.toml\") as f:\n   112→              for line in f:\n   113→                  line = line.strip()\n   114→                  m = re.match(r'^\\[defaults\\]', line)\n   115→                  if m:\n   116→                      current_crate = \"__defaults__\"\n   117→                      continue\n   118→                  m = re.match(r'^\\[crates\\.(\\w+)\\]', line)\n   119→                  if m:\n   120→                      current_crate = m.group(1)\n   121→                      continue\n   122→                  m = re.match(r'^max_regression_pct\\s*=\\s*(\\d+)', line)\n   123→                  if m:\n   124→                      val = int(m.group(1))\n   125→                      if current_crate == \"__defaults__\":\n   126→                          default_pct = val\n   127→                      elif current_crate:\n   128→                          thresholds[current_crate] = val\n   129→\n   130→          # Map benchmark group names to crate names\n   131→          group_to_crate = {\n   132→              \"insert\": \"relational_engine\",\n   133→              \"batch_insert\": \"relational_engine\",\n   134→              \"select\": \"relational_engine\",\n   135→              \"aggregation\": \"relational_engine\",\n   136→              \"group_by\": \"relational_engine\",\n   137→              \"join\": \"relational_engine\",\n   138→              \"create_nodes\": \"graph_engine\",\n   139→              \"create_edges\": \"graph_engine\",\n   140→              \"neighbors\": \"graph_engine\",\n   141→              \"traverse\": \"graph_engine\",\n   142→              \"find_path\": \"graph_engine\",\n   143→              \"weighted_shortest_path\": \"graph_engine\",\n   144→              \"store_embedding\": \"vector_engine\",\n   145→              \"search_similar\": \"vector_engine\",\n   146→              \"metric_comparison\": \"vector_engine\",\n   147→              \"hnsw\": \"vector_engine\",\n   148→              \"tensor_store\": \"tensor_store\",\n   149→              \"tensor_compress\": \"tensor_compress\",\n   150→              \"tensor_chain\": \"tensor_chain\",\n   151→              \"distributed\": \"tensor_chain\",\n   152→              \"tensor_vault\": \"tensor_vault\",\n   153→              \"tensor_cache\": \"tensor_cache\",\n   154→              \"tensor_blob\": \"tensor_blob\",\n   155→              \"blob\": \"tensor_blob\",\n   156→              \"neumann_parser\": \"neumann_parser\",\n   157→              \"query_router\": \"query_router\",\n   158→              \"neumann_shell\": \"neumann\",\n   159→              \"neumann_server\": \"neumann_server\",\n   160→              \"tensor_unified\": \"tensor_unified\",\n   161→              \"tensor_checkpoint\": \"tensor_checkpoint\",\n   162→              \"checkpoint\": \"tensor_checkpoint\",\n   163→          }\n   164→\n   165→          violations = []\n   166→          with open(\"bench-comparison.txt\") as f:\n   167→              for line in f:\n   168→                  # Match: group/bench base 1.234ms pr 1.500ms +21.55%\n   169→                  m = re.search(r'\\+(\\d+\\.?\\d*)%', line)\n   170→                  if not m:\n   171→                      continue\n   172→                  pct = float(m.group(1))\n   173→                  # Extract group name (first column, before /)\n   174→                  parts = line.strip().split()\n   175→                  if not parts:\n   176→                      continue\n   177→                  bench_name = parts[0]\n   178→                  group = bench_name.split(\"/\")[0] \\\n   179→                      if \"/\" in bench_name else bench_name\n   180→\n   181→                  # Find crate for this group\n   182→                  crate_name = None\n   183→                  for prefix, crate in group_to_crate.items():\n   184→                      if group.startswith(prefix):\n   185→                          crate_name = crate\n   186→                          break\n   187→\n   188→                  threshold = thresholds.get(\n   189→                      crate_name, default_pct\n   190→                  ) if crate_name else default_pct\n   191→                  if pct >= threshold:\n   192→                      violations.append(\n   193→                          f\"{bench_name}: +{pct:.1f}%\"\n   194→                          f\" (threshold: {threshold}%)\"\n   195→                      )\n   196→\n   197→          with open(\"regression-report.txt\", \"w\") as f:\n   198→              if violations:\n   199→                  f.write(\"REGRESSIONS DETECTED:\\n\")\n   200→                  for v in violations:\n   201→                      f.write(f\"  {v}\\n\")\n   202→              else:\n   203→                  f.write(\"No significant regressions.\\n\")\n   204→\n   205→          sys.exit(0)\n   206→          PYEOF\n   207→\n   208→          HAS_REGRESSIONS=false\n   209→          if grep -q \"REGRESSIONS DETECTED\" regression-report.txt; then\n   210→            HAS_REGRESSIONS=true\n   211→          fi\n   212→\n   213→          {\n   214→            echo \"comparison<<EOF\"\n   215→            cat bench-comparison.txt\n   216→            echo \"EOF\"\n   217→            echo \"regression_report<<REOF\"\n   218→            cat regression-report.txt\n   219→            echo \"REOF\"\n   220→            echo \"has_regressions=$HAS_REGRESSIONS\"\n   221→          } >> \"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"\n   222→\n   223→      - name: Post benchmark results\n   224→        # v7.0.1\n   225→        uses: actions/github-script@ed597411d8f924073f98dfc5c65a23a2325f34cd\n   226→        with:\n   227→          script: |\n   228→            const comparison = `${{ steps.compare.outputs.comparison }}`;\n   229→            const regressionReport =\n   230→              `${{ steps.compare.outputs.regression_report }}`;\n   231→            const hasRegressions = ${{ steps.compare.outputs.has_regressions }};\n   232→\n   233→            let body = '## Benchmark Results\\n\\n';\n   234→\n   235→            if (hasRegressions) {\n   236→              body += '> [!WARNING]\\n';\n   237→              body += '> Per-crate regression thresholds exceeded\\n\\n';\n   238→              body += '```\\n' + regressionReport + '\\n```\\n\\n';\n   239→            }\n   240→\n   241→            body += '<details>\\n<summary>Full comparison</summary>\\n\\n';\n   242→            body += '```\\n' + comparison + '\\n```\\n\\n';\n   243→            body += '</details>\\n\\n';\n   244→            const prSha = context.sha.substring(0, 7);\n   245→            const pr = context.payload.pull_request;\n   246→            const baseSha = pr.base.sha.substring(0, 7);\n   247→            body += `_Benchmarks: \\`${prSha}\\` vs \\`${baseSha}\\`_`;\n   248→\n   249→            const { data: comments } = await github.rest.issues.listComments({\n   250→              owner: context.repo.owner,\n   251→              repo: context.repo.repo,\n   252→              issue_number: context.issue.number\n   253→            });\n   254→\n   255→            const existingComment = comments.find(c =>\n   256→              c.user.type === 'Bot' &&\n   257→              c.body.includes('## Benchmark Results')\n   258→            );\n   259→\n   260→            if (existingComment) {\n   261→              await github.rest.issues.updateComment({\n   262→                owner: context.repo.owner,\n   263→                repo: context.repo.repo,\n   264→                comment_id: existingComment.id,\n   265→                body: body\n   266→              });\n   267→            } else {\n   268→              await github.rest.issues.createComment({\n   269→                owner: context.repo.owner,\n   270→                repo: context.repo.repo,\n   271→                issue_number: context.issue.number,\n   272→                body: body\n   273→              });\n   274→            }\n   275→"}]},"uuid":"646e74a5-a824-49c0-8c61-0adb2a22185c","timestamp":"2026-03-12T19:05:54.101Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/lukin/Neumann/.github/workflows/bench-pr.yml","content":"---\nname: Benchmark PR\n\n\"on\":\n  pull_request:\n    types: [labeled, opened, synchronize]\n    paths:\n      - 'tensor_store/src/**'\n      - 'relational_engine/src/**'\n      - 'graph_engine/src/**'\n      - 'vector_engine/src/**'\n      - 'tensor_chain/src/**'\n      - 'query_router/src/**'\n      - '**/benches/**'\n\npermissions:\n  contents: read\n  pull-requests: write\n\njobs:\n  benchmark:\n    name: Run Benchmarks\n    if: >-\n      github.event.label.name == 'bench' ||\n      (github.event_name == 'pull_request' && github.event.action != 'labeled')\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    timeout-minutes: 45\n    steps:\n      - name: Checkout PR\n        # v4.2.2\n        uses: actions/checkout@de0fac2e4500dabe0009e67214ff5f5447ce83dd\n\n      - name: Try to download main baseline\n        id: baseline\n        # v4.3.0\n        uses: >-\n          actions/download-artifact@d3f86a106a0bac45b974a628896c90dbdf5c8093\n        continue-on-error: true\n        with:\n          name: criterion-baseline\n          path: target/criterion\n          github-token: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}\n          repository: ${{ github.repository }}\n          run-id: ${{ github.event.pull_request.base.sha }}\n\n      - name: Checkout base branch (fallback)\n        if: steps.baseline.outcome == 'failure'\n        # v4.2.2\n        uses: actions/checkout@de0fac2e4500dabe0009e67214ff5f5447ce83dd\n        with:\n          ref: ${{ github.base_ref }}\n          path: base\n\n      - name: Install Rust toolchain\n        # stable\n        uses: dtolnay/rust-toolchain@f7ccc83f9ed1e5b9c81d8a67d7ad1a747e22a561\n        with:\n          toolchain: stable\n\n      - name: Cache Rust\n        # v2.7.8\n        uses: Swatinem/rust-cache@779680da715d629ac1d338a641029a2f4372abb5\n\n      - name: Install protoc\n        run: >-\n          sudo apt-get update &&\n          sudo apt-get install -y protobuf-compiler\n\n      - name: Install critcmp\n        run: cargo install critcmp\n\n      - name: Benchmark base branch (fallback)\n        if: steps.baseline.outcome == 'failure'\n        working-directory: base\n        run: |\n          cargo bench --workspace --bench '*' \\\n            --exclude fuzz \\\n            --exclude neumann-native \\\n            --exclude integration_tests \\\n            --exclude stress_tests \\\n            -- --save-baseline base\n\n      - name: Copy cached baseline\n        if: steps.baseline.outcome == 'success'\n        run: |\n          echo \"Using cached main baseline from artifact\"\n\n      - name: Benchmark PR branch\n        run: |\n          cargo bench --workspace --bench '*' \\\n            --exclude fuzz \\\n            --exclude neumann-native \\\n            --exclude integration_tests \\\n            --exclude stress_tests \\\n            -- --save-baseline pr\n\n      - name: Compare benchmarks with per-crate thresholds\n        id: compare\n        run: |\n          critcmp base pr > bench-comparison.txt 2>&1 || true\n\n          python3 - << 'PYEOF'\n          import re\n          import sys\n\n          # Parse bench-thresholds.toml for per-crate thresholds\n          thresholds = {}\n          default_pct = 15\n          current_crate = None\n\n          with open(\"bench-thresholds.toml\") as f:\n              for line in f:\n                  line = line.strip()\n                  m = re.match(r'^\\[defaults\\]', line)\n                  if m:\n                      current_crate = \"__defaults__\"\n                      continue\n                  m = re.match(r'^\\[crates\\.(\\w+)\\]', line)\n                  if m:\n                      current_crate = m.group(1)\n                      continue\n                  m = re.match(r'^max_regression_pct\\s*=\\s*(\\d+)', line)\n                  if m:\n                      val = int(m.group(1))\n                      if current_crate == \"__defaults__\":\n                          default_pct = val\n                      elif current_crate:\n                          thresholds[current_crate] = val\n\n          # Map benchmark group names to crate names\n          group_to_crate = {\n              \"insert\": \"relational_engine\",\n              \"batch_insert\": \"relational_engine\",\n              \"select\": \"relational_engine\",\n              \"aggregation\": \"relational_engine\",\n              \"group_by\": \"relational_engine\",\n              \"join\": \"relational_engine\",\n              \"create_nodes\": \"graph_engine\",\n              \"create_edges\": \"graph_engine\",\n              \"neighbors\": \"graph_engine\",\n              \"traverse\": \"graph_engine\",\n              \"find_path\": \"graph_engine\",\n              \"weighted_shortest_path\": \"graph_engine\",\n              \"store_embedding\": \"vector_engine\",\n              \"search_similar\": \"vector_engine\",\n              \"metric_comparison\": \"vector_engine\",\n              \"hnsw\": \"vector_engine\",\n              \"tensor_store\": \"tensor_store\",\n              \"tensor_compress\": \"tensor_compress\",\n              \"tensor_chain\": \"tensor_chain\",\n              \"distributed\": \"tensor_chain\",\n              \"tensor_vault\": \"tensor_vault\",\n              \"tensor_cache\": \"tensor_cache\",\n              \"tensor_blob\": \"tensor_blob\",\n              \"blob\": \"tensor_blob\",\n              \"neumann_parser\": \"neumann_parser\",\n              \"query_router\": \"query_router\",\n              \"neumann_shell\": \"neumann\",\n              \"neumann_server\": \"neumann_server\",\n              \"tensor_unified\": \"tensor_unified\",\n              \"tensor_checkpoint\": \"tensor_checkpoint\",\n              \"checkpoint\": \"tensor_checkpoint\",\n          }\n\n          violations = []\n          with open(\"bench-comparison.txt\") as f:\n              for line in f:\n                  # Match: group/bench base 1.234ms pr 1.500ms +21.55%\n                  m = re.search(r'\\+(\\d+\\.?\\d*)%', line)\n                  if not m:\n                      continue\n                  pct = float(m.group(1))\n                  # Extract group name (first column, before /)\n                  parts = line.strip().split()\n                  if not parts:\n                      continue\n                  bench_name = parts[0]\n                  group = bench_name.split(\"/\")[0] \\\n                      if \"/\" in bench_name else bench_name\n\n                  # Find crate for this group\n                  crate_name = None\n                  for prefix, crate in group_to_crate.items():\n                      if group.startswith(prefix):\n                          crate_name = crate\n                          break\n\n                  threshold = thresholds.get(\n                      crate_name, default_pct\n                  ) if crate_name else default_pct\n                  if pct >= threshold:\n                      violations.append(\n                          f\"{bench_name}: +{pct:.1f}%\"\n                          f\" (threshold: {threshold}%)\"\n                      )\n\n          with open(\"regression-report.txt\", \"w\") as f:\n              if violations:\n                  f.write(\"REGRESSIONS DETECTED:\\n\")\n                  for v in violations:\n                      f.write(f\"  {v}\\n\")\n              else:\n                  f.write(\"No significant regressions.\\n\")\n\n          sys.exit(0)\n          PYEOF\n\n          HAS_REGRESSIONS=false\n          if grep -q \"REGRESSIONS DETECTED\" regression-report.txt; then\n            HAS_REGRESSIONS=true\n          fi\n\n          {\n            echo \"comparison<<EOF\"\n            cat bench-comparison.txt\n            echo \"EOF\"\n            echo \"regression_report<<REOF\"\n            cat regression-report.txt\n            echo \"REOF\"\n            echo \"has_regressions=$HAS_REGRESSIONS\"\n          } >> \"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"\n\n      - name: Post benchmark results\n        # v7.0.1\n        uses: actions/github-script@ed597411d8f924073f98dfc5c65a23a2325f34cd\n        with:\n          script: |\n            const comparison = `${{ steps.compare.outputs.comparison }}`;\n            const regressionReport =\n              `${{ steps.compare.outputs.regression_report }}`;\n            const hasRegressions = ${{ steps.compare.outputs.has_regressions }};\n\n            let body = '## Benchmark Results\\n\\n';\n\n            if (hasRegressions) {\n              body += '> [!WARNING]\\n';\n              body += '> Per-crate regression thresholds exceeded\\n\\n';\n              body += '```\\n' + regressionReport + '\\n```\\n\\n';\n            }\n\n            body += '<details>\\n<summary>Full comparison</summary>\\n\\n';\n            body += '```\\n' + comparison + '\\n```\\n\\n';\n            body += '</details>\\n\\n';\n            const prSha = context.sha.substring(0, 7);\n            const pr = context.payload.pull_request;\n            const baseSha = pr.base.sha.substring(0, 7);\n            body += `_Benchmarks: \\`${prSha}\\` vs \\`${baseSha}\\`_`;\n\n            const { data: comments } = await github.rest.issues.listComments({\n              owner: context.repo.owner,\n              repo: context.repo.repo,\n              issue_number: context.issue.number\n            });\n\n            const existingComment = comments.find(c =>\n              c.user.type === 'Bot' &&\n              c.body.includes('## Benchmark Results')\n            );\n\n            if (existingComment) {\n              await github.rest.issues.updateComment({\n                owner: context.repo.owner,\n                repo: context.repo.repo,\n                comment_id: existingComment.id,\n                body: body\n              });\n            } else {\n              await github.rest.issues.createComment({\n                owner: context.repo.owner,\n                repo: context.repo.repo,\n                issue_number: context.issue.number,\n                body: body\n              });\n            }\n","numLines":275,"startLine":1,"totalLines":275}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bc467ea0-74e6-4d0c-b382-6877b1ae1514"}
